@3. The modules
.
=3. THE MODULES
.
.Each table is in (set before the GOSUB), out (read after it), and internal
.(do not read, do not write, do not rely on).
.
=THEME.INC.BL -- named colour roles
.
.Routines, arguments and examples: SEC 4.1.
.
.  in
.      THEME.ID -- 0 x16, 1 dark, 2 light, 3 gray, 4 custom, read by
.        THEME.SELECT
.      THEME.ATTR -- a packed attribute, for THEME.SET and THEME.HI
.
.  out
.      THEME.CLR(role) -- the colour array, DIMmed to THEME.SLOTS
.      THEME.INV -- the inverse attribute, from THEME.HI
.
.  internal
.      THEME.READY
.
.  constants
.      THEME.PAGE THEME.TEXT THEME.TITLE THEME.BORDER THEME.HILITE
.        THEME.DIMMED THEME.WARN THEME.FOCUS THEME.SLOTS THEME.COUNT
.
.To use it: set THEME.ID, GOSUB THEME.SELECT, then index THEME.CLR() with a
.role wherever a drawing routine wants an attribute. SEC 4.1 is the module's
.own entry, with the five themes and the other four routines.
.
:THEME.ID = 1 : GOSUB THEME.SELECT
:GP.PRINTAT 2, 2, "READY", THEME.CLR(THEME.TEXT)
.
.THEME.CLR is the array this module DIMs. Do not DIM it yourself -- the
.module owns it, and DIMming an array GPC has already dimensioned is an
.error.
.
.THEME.FOCUS is the eighth role and the newest: the attribute a focused
.control wears while GUI.FORM has the keyboard. THEME.SLOTS is 8 because of
.it, and THEME.COUNT stays 5 -- the first is how many roles there are, the
.second how many themes.
.
=APPSYS.INC.BL -- start politely, leave it as you found it
.
.Routines, arguments and examples: SEC 4.3.
.
.  in
.      APPSYS.FILE$ APPSYS.BANK APPSYS.X APPSYS.Y APPSYS.W APPSYS.H
.        APPSYS.DEV -- the panel routines
.
.  out
.      APPSYS.MODE APPSYS.COLS APPSYS.ROWS APPSYS.COLOUR -- set by
.        APPSYS.STARTUP
.      APPSYS.IS.EMULATOR -- set by APPSYS.ISEMU
.
.  internal
.      APPSYS.LAST
.
.  constants
.      APPSYS.SCRMODE APPSYS.COLREG APPSYS.SETCHR APPSYS.CHRREG APPSYS.EMUSIG
.
.Lay the screen out from APPSYS.COLS and APPSYS.ROWS. Do not assume 80x60 --
.the X16 boots there but SCREEN 0 is 40x30, and someone who prefers larger
.text is running one.
.
=STRINGS.INC.BL -- string helpers
.
.Routines, arguments and examples: SEC 4.2.
.
.  in
.      STR.STR$ -- the string, in and out
.      STR.WIDTH -- field width, the pad routines
.      STR.DELIM$ STR.MAX -- SPLIT (MAX 0 means 10)
.      STR.FIND$ STR.REPL$ -- REPLACE
.      STR.PET -- a PETSCII code, PET2SCR
.      STR.AT STR.CUT STR.SUB$ -- SPLICE, and AT/CUT are CLAMPED in place
.      STR.PTR -- GP.STRPTR of the string, the three trims
.
.  out
.      STR.STR$ -- padded, or replaced, in place
.      STR.N -- how many fields SPLIT found, always >= 1
.      STR.FIELD$(1..N) -- the fields themselves
.      STR.SCR -- the screen code from PET2SCR
.      STR.STR$ -- spliced, when it was SPLICE that was called
.
.  internal
.      STR.GAP STR.HALF STR.REST$ STR.AT STR.LIM STR.OUT$
.      STR.ADDR% STR.OP% STR.KEEP% -- the {VAR} slots the trim blob reads
.
.STR.FIELD$ is the one array the library does not DIM. Left alone, GPC's
.implicit DIM gives 0..10. For more, DIM it before the first call and set
.STR.MAX to match -- DIMming an array GPC has already auto-dimensioned is an
.error, so it is one or the other. This is the opposite of THEME.CLR, which
.the module owns outright; the two are worth keeping straight.
.
